WEBVTT

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:04.240
2012 AD.

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:07.180
Mankind began the interstellar migration to

00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:12.150
and the colonization of habitable planets they found across the galaxy.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:18.950
However, a good number of those planets are already inhabited by indigenous groups.

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:25.420
The children of the Protoculture, the advanced 
civilization that sowed the seeds of life across the galaxy,

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:33.350
have met again after several tens of thousands of years.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.600
Children of the Protoculture!

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:40.210
We, the Windermere Kingdom,

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:44.600
hereby declare war on the New Unified Government!

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:46.540
But why?

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:55.360
Forty years ago, the New Unified Government reached out to us Windermereans.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:01:00.330
However, under their cooperative guise hid true evil.

00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:06.540
They crafted a profoundly unequal treaty and sought to monopolize all profits.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:12.760
Having struggled for many long decades, we rose up against this foe seven years ago

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:17.340
and successfully took back our mother sky.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:22.090
Nevertheless, as long as they exist in this Brisingr Globular Cluster,

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:23.930
we may never find true peace!

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:29.610
Rise and spread your wings to freedom!

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:33.060
<i>We've only got one shot at love,</i>

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:35.920
<i>so let's have fun inside of you</i>

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:39.780
<i>Let's share a selfish kiss</i>

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:50.580
<i>The petals of this flower fall in the wind</i>

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:56.050
<i>The stars are more than I could count</i>

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:59.590
<i>It doesn't matter if I blame it all on you,</i>

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:02.340
<i>swallowing back my tears</i>

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:07.180
<i>I can't tell anyone about how my heart races</i>

00:02:07.180 --> 00:02:09.390
<i>Reach out</i>

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:10.730
<i>Until it all breaks apart</i>

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:12.640
<i>Reach out</i>

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:13.870
<i>Until you can take flight</i>

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:15.360
<i>To the ends</i>

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:16.190
<i>Deep in my heart</i>

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.980
<i>Of time</i>

00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:18.780
<i>There is a prayer</i>

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:21.700
<i>Just feel, just believe</i>

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:25.800
<i>and speed through it all</i>

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.950
<i>We've only got one shot at love,</i>

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:31.710
<i>so let's have fun inside of you</i>

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:37.290
<i>Let's share a kiss faster than light, just wait for me</i>

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.920
<i>My body almost forgot</i>

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:42.930
<i>My heart kept beating loudly</i>

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:48.360
<i>Escape your chains, they're all but a dream</i>

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:55.070
<i>Tear them off and come at me, just like that</i>

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:05.190
You can't adblock this!

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:29.890
Buy the singles!

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:44.030
It's goodyummy!

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:46.660
Jellyfish chips is like crack.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:47.720
Indeed!

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:50.120
Not to mention it's the spicy limited edition.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:00.490
Sorry for the wait.

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:05.310
Windermere is 800 light years from Ragna.

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:08.680
It is a planet with a dimensional barrier around it.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:12.230
Moving on, these new units are the SV-262 Draken III.

00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:16.590
The ones piloting them are the Aerial Knights of Windermere.

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:19.380
They're winged knights who serve the royal family.

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:25.510
Judging by the movement patterns, that's gotta be the White Knight of Darwent.

00:04:25.510 --> 00:04:26.410
White Knight?

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:30.700
It's the title that's passed on to the ace pilot of the Aerial Knights.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:33.770
White? Not black?

00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:36.880
The unit used to be colored in silver.

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.880
Some paths are bound to cross again.

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:46.470
Were you by any chance on Windermere at some point?

00:04:46.980 --> 00:04:49.180
Yeah. Seven years ago.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:52.220
During their war of independence.

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:56.230
Were they the ones controlling the Spacy pilots?

00:04:56.570 --> 00:04:57.690
Most likely.

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:02.330
So they were involved in all the previous Var outbreaks?

00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:06.160
Not all, but they were involved in some.

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:10.580
HQ mentioned only cases with powerful bio-fold waves detected could be attributed to them.

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:12.380
Up until now, they've been...

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:13.200
Experiments.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:14.830
Most recently,

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:20.420
they were able to work together instead of merely being reduced to a mindless mob.

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:22.880
That's my guess, at least.

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:29.140
However, on Vordor, the majority of Spacy units fell under their control

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:31.640
and the planet essentially surrendered without any resistance.

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:33.720
They conquered a planet without a fight?

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:35.730
But how?

00:05:36.010 --> 00:05:37.650
I heard a song.

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:39.150
A song?

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:41.880
Yeah. Someone was singing.

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:44.140
It was a beautiful voice, but...

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:46.360
It tingled and it sounded painful...

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:50.010
It was the voice of a boy.

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:52.170
A boy?

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:55.040
Actually, I think you're right.

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:57.790
Kaname, did you hear it too?

00:05:58.290 --> 00:05:59.250
Yeah.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:01.960
Is he an angel? Or a devil?

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:10.760
He so quickly made so many Var infected his puppets.

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:13.060
Isn't that quite impressive?

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:16.320
Could you hear it?

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:19.980
No. Perhaps only Walkure members could?

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:21.730
I heard it as well.

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:23.480
Seriously?

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:27.990
But I'd rather say I felt it instead of hearing it.

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:35.650
A voice that travels faster than light and even beyond dimensions...

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:38.250
Sounds like a Wind Singer.

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:39.760
What's that?

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:43.880
A Windermerean legend.

00:06:43.880 --> 00:06:47.880
Yup. About runes and the light of life.

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:51.980
Wind Singer?

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:58.270
Planet Windermere

00:07:01.640 --> 00:07:04.120
The Knights are back!

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:07.890
It's the White Knight!

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:23.040
You freed two planets?

00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:24.480
Yes.

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:27.440
We successfully controlled the 
Var with the song of the wind.

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:31.470
This is the first step to securing the domain of the wind.

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:36.310
However, doing so has strained Prince Heinz much more than expected.

00:07:36.750 --> 00:07:42.230
We also need more time to analyze the capabilities of the relics, which includes the Shrine of Time.

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:45.190
I fear that we need to reconsider our strategy.

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:49.890
Fear not. The wind will surely blow

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:54.110
and bring destruction upon the earthlings.

00:07:54.950 --> 00:07:56.240
Most definitely.

00:07:58.030 --> 00:08:02.470
Even though he says that, His Majesty is in frail health...

00:08:02.470 --> 00:08:04.650
Reconsider our strategy?

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:11.220
If you're worrying about His Majesty and Prince Heinz, do realize how little time we have.

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:13.720
We should've finished them off.

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:17.100
Our objective is not bloodshed.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:20.670
As the legitimate heirs of the Protoculture.

00:08:20.670 --> 00:08:25.600
we must guide the people of the 
Globular Cluster down the right path.

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:31.800
Your sword has become rusty.

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:35.320
It is time, Casim.

00:08:35.320 --> 00:08:41.500
Yes. Still, it took us seven years to ready our wings.

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:49.860
I'm already 23. I don't know if 
I can fly until the end of all this.

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:53.420
Please, I'm 33 and—

00:09:03.320 --> 00:09:05.480
Perfection as usual, Master Hermann.

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:08.090
I'm not your master anymore.

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:10.860
How long are you going to keep up this game?

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:14.030
Until I can land a hit, of course.

00:09:15.010 --> 00:09:17.650
More importantly, please take a look at this.

00:09:18.680 --> 00:09:21.270
Is that a rune?

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:24.250
I smell the pungent winds of a traitor.

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:27.390
How old are you? Control your runes.

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:35.720
A Windermerean in Walkure...

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:38.220
Planet Ragna

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:40.300
Our client's requirements have changed?

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:44.180
It's from the autonomous government of the Ragna system.

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:48.520
Up until now, our job was to handle the Var riots.

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:53.860
In addition, we must now partake in the defense 
against the advances of the Windermere Kingdom.

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:57.340
In other words, we're going to war.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:10:01.120
Accordingly, we'll update the 
terms of our contracts as well.

00:10:01.530 --> 00:10:03.740
Remember, Chaos is a civilian contractor.

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:07.500
If you disagree with the new 
terms, you are free to leave.

00:10:07.700 --> 00:10:09.380
Of course I'll stay.

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:10.500
Same here.

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:11.960
A pointless question.

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:16.110
I can't just leave my cute little Siegfrieds, can I now?

00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:17.780
You spoke our minds, Makina!

00:10:17.780 --> 00:10:19.140
We'll follow you no matter what!

00:10:19.650 --> 00:10:20.590
I'm staying.

00:10:20.840 --> 00:10:23.950
Not to mention I've yet to date anyone here!

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:24.790
What do you say?

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:25.560
Should we quit?

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:28.060
Ready to put my seal on it.

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:29.890
Oh, please.

00:10:29.890 --> 00:10:31.920
Hayate, what about you?

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:35.780
Give it some thought.

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:39.470
Speaking of which, what are you going to do?

00:10:41.010 --> 00:10:45.250
To be perfectly honest, I've got no idea what war is.

00:10:45.250 --> 00:10:48.330
Is that so? There's a problem, however.

00:10:48.740 --> 00:10:52.620
The Chaos HQ is suspecting that you're a spy.

00:10:52.620 --> 00:10:53.920
A s-spy?!

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:55.710
Mikumo!

00:10:56.420 --> 00:10:59.840
The media and fans all share similar sentiments.

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:05.090
Well, it's definitely more interesting with a spy on board,

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:07.310
but if you consider how they'll resp—

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:13.650
It's okay! I'll do all I can and some 
more so that they'd believe in me!

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:18.150
Is that so? I'm looking forward to that.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:29.830
Gramia Nehrich Windermere,

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:32.610
a ghost from seven years ago.

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:35.090
Shall we?

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:37.880
Yeah...

00:11:55.430 --> 00:11:57.480
I've got a bad feeling...

00:11:58.440 --> 00:11:59.610
I knew it.

00:12:00.700 --> 00:12:03.240
You like the wind here, too?

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:13.290
War, huh?

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:25.800
While you're at it, buy some Blu-rays too!

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:31.350
Sign: Ragnyannyan

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:36.270
Look at that now.

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:38.320
Is it an upgrade to the multi-drone plate?

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:43.940
Yeah. We'll have to work even better in sync with the Delta Platoon.

00:12:46.930 --> 00:12:49.270
War? You're overreacting.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:52.190
But haven't you heard the rumors?

00:12:52.190 --> 00:12:54.870
Perhaps we should go back earlier.

00:12:55.570 --> 00:12:56.830
Say, Mirage.

00:12:57.150 --> 00:13:00.210
Have you ever fought wars against humans?

00:13:01.800 --> 00:13:06.640
Yes, I have when I was in the Spacy.

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:07.510
You, Lt. Chuck?

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:09.680
I have too.

00:13:10.250 --> 00:13:12.810
Do you know about Windermere's war of independence?

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:17.440
That they used a dimensional weapon which resulted in an armistice that has lasted ever since?

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:20.400
I don't know the exact details either.

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:25.150
When they declared war a few days ago, they 
claimed the N.U.G. was taking advantage of them.

00:13:25.460 --> 00:13:28.670
We're talking politics between different planets.

00:13:28.670 --> 00:13:30.330
Things aren't black and white.

00:13:31.350 --> 00:13:34.730
Miramira, it's good to have these serious discussions,

00:13:34.730 --> 00:13:36.420
but you should first fill up yourself.

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:38.750
Food should be enjoyed.

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:40.170
You're right. I'm diggin' in!

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:46.380
Hey, you're late! Where'd you go?

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:47.380
Just walking around.

00:13:49.990 --> 00:13:55.850
Exactly! Windermere is extremely strict with their border controls.

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:59.060
You can't just <i>leave</i> to join Walkure. It's nonsense.

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:02.310
Not exactly trustworthy.

00:14:02.310 --> 00:14:04.110
You're famous, Freyja!

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:05.360
Yeah!

00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:07.780
What do I do now?

00:14:08.690 --> 00:14:10.080
There she is!

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:15.020
You're Freyja Wion, right?

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:16.570
May we have a word please?

00:14:16.570 --> 00:14:17.410
Look here!

00:14:17.760 --> 00:14:19.210
What's the ruckus?

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:21.290
There have been rumors that you're a spy.

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:23.210
Why did you join Walkure?

00:14:23.430 --> 00:14:26.970
Is it true that you're associated with the Windermerean military?

00:14:28.180 --> 00:14:30.930
Please give us an answer, Freyja!

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:33.390
Cut it out, you guys!

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:35.060
Get out if you're not buying anything!

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:37.560
It's rude to interrupt someone else's dinner!

00:14:38.630 --> 00:14:40.430
That's Makina Nakajima!

00:14:40.430 --> 00:14:42.090
And Reina Prowler!

00:14:42.090 --> 00:14:43.150
This has gotten bad.

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:44.990
What are your thoughts, Makina?

00:14:44.990 --> 00:14:46.600
Please say something, Reina!

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:48.440
Let's go.

00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:50.040
Wait!

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:51.190
Are you running away?

00:14:51.190 --> 00:14:52.840
Tell us the truth!

00:14:52.840 --> 00:14:54.250
Freyja!

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:05.130
I'm not used to running so much. I'm exhausted!

00:15:05.480 --> 00:15:07.480
Don't push yourself.

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:10.590
I'm not push—

00:15:12.990 --> 00:15:15.240
Where do you think you're touching me, you perv!

00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:16.890
Don't push yourself.

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:20.370
Your horn is still blue.

00:15:21.120 --> 00:15:23.890
If you're gonna lie, at least be good at it.

00:15:23.890 --> 00:15:27.150
It's annoying how obvious it is that you're just acting tough.

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:29.070
Is it really that obvious?

00:15:29.330 --> 00:15:31.430
Everyone can see right through you.

00:15:38.320 --> 00:15:40.500
I want to stay in Walkure.

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:45.780
But I can't stop worrying about the people in my village back on Windermere.

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:51.670
Jeez! Why the heck do they have to go to war again?!

00:15:54.660 --> 00:15:57.810
Why can't everyone just get along?

00:15:59.160 --> 00:16:01.310
My grandfather was an earthling,

00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:03.730
and my grandmother a Zentradi.

00:16:04.000 --> 00:16:05.510
Mirage?

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:10.360
They were the first such interspecies couple in history.

00:16:10.920 --> 00:16:15.420
Even worse, their species were at war with each other at the time.

00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:18.830
Nonetheless, they married each other

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:22.260
and showed everyone how earthlings and Zentradi can live together in peace.

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:24.430
And?

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:27.190
What's your point?

00:16:27.190 --> 00:16:30.840
"Just like my wonderful grandparents,

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:35.090
you too should become a bridge that 
connects species." Something like that?

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:37.440
I didn't mean...

00:16:37.440 --> 00:16:41.220
Aren't you putting a bit too much pressure on Freyja now?

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:42.230
That's not what I meant!

00:16:42.420 --> 00:16:49.710
I heard that your grandparents were legendary ace pilots.

00:16:51.170 --> 00:16:53.790
Putting me and my ancestry aside, what about you?

00:16:53.790 --> 00:16:56.010
Are you going to stay with the Delta Platoon?

00:16:56.010 --> 00:16:57.820
Don't change the topic.

00:16:57.820 --> 00:16:59.720
I would've guessed you're not staying.

00:16:59.720 --> 00:17:02.960
Ragna has lots of mercats and you're allergic to cats.

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:05.540
You even keep getting destroyed by a stray one.

00:17:05.540 --> 00:17:07.170
I'm gonna roast it next time!

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:09.290
That's hard to believe.

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:12.130
At least I don't smell like puke.

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:14.770
It was your puke!

00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:21.270
Oh man, whatever.

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:22.700
Come, Freyja.

00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:24.310
Where to?

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:25.870
I'll show you a nice place.

00:17:30.340 --> 00:17:31.980
I don't care anymore!

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:38.370
That's a deculture and a half!

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:40.740
Is it all right to do this without permission?

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:43.140
Don't worry. I'm just practicing.

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:45.460
Not to mention we both needed to clear our heads.

00:17:47.110 --> 00:17:48.460
You're right.

00:17:49.230 --> 00:17:50.840
Need some fresh air for that!

00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:54.420
Shall we?

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:56.620
Let's go!

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:14.860
This is like some fairy tale, flying the skies of Ragna with just the two of us.

00:18:16.310 --> 00:18:20.190
You have such a creepy laugh.

00:18:20.190 --> 00:18:22.830
Say that again to my face!

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:26.870
That's why you're not popular with the ladies.

00:18:26.870 --> 00:18:28.470
Sure.

00:18:31.780 --> 00:18:34.880
Anyway... thank you.

